WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.300 --> 00:00:02.202 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Three children, yes?
-I have three of them, yes.

00:00:02.202 --> 00:00:03.269 line:92%
-And do they know your work?

00:00:03.269 --> 00:00:05.372 align:start size:94% position:6%
Because I would assume
that once they do,

00:00:05.372 --> 00:00:07.307 align:start size:94% position:6%
they will enjoy it
a great deal.

00:00:07.307 --> 00:00:09.642 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Well, I thought
I should tell them

00:00:09.642 --> 00:00:11.211 align:start size:94% position:6%
what Dada does for a living.
-Yeah.

00:00:11.211 --> 00:00:13.480 align:start size:94% position:6%
-I had seen --
not in terms of scale,

00:00:13.480 --> 00:00:17.250 align:start size:94% position:6%
but I had seen Dhani Harrison
talking about his dad,

00:00:17.250 --> 00:00:19.853 align:start size:94% position:6%
George Harrison,
that he went to school,

00:00:19.853 --> 00:00:21.454 align:start size:94% position:6%
and for the longest time
he didn't know

00:00:21.454 --> 00:00:22.789 align:start size:94% position:6%
that his dad was
in The Beatles.

00:00:22.789 --> 00:00:24.624 size:84% position:42%
And so people would go,
"Your dad's a Beatle."

00:00:24.624 --> 00:00:26.292 align:start size:94% position:6%
And he would go, "Shut up!"
[ Laughter ]

00:00:26.292 --> 00:00:29.763 align:start size:94% position:6%
And then he came home
and said to George Harrison,

00:00:29.763 --> 00:00:31.064 align:start size:94% position:6%
"Are you a Beatle?"
And he goes,

00:00:31.064 --> 00:00:32.866 size:84% position:42%
[ As George Harrison ]
"Yeah, I am, actually."

00:00:32.866 --> 00:00:34.534 align:start size:94% position:6%
I go,
"Why didn't you tell him?"

00:00:34.534 --> 00:00:37.103 align:start size:94% position:6%
He goes, "I suppose I should
have, really."

00:00:37.103 --> 00:00:39.506 align:start size:94% position:6%
[ Laughter ]
And I thought, well,

00:00:39.506 --> 00:00:40.507 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
I'll tell them.

00:00:40.507 --> 00:00:42.108 size:81% position:41% line:92%
I'm not a -- a Beatle.

00:00:42.108 --> 00:00:44.310 align:start size:94% position:6%
But, you know, I make stuff.
-Yeah.

00:00:44.310 --> 00:00:47.080 align:start size:94% position:6%
-And so, I told him,
and we let him watch it,

00:00:47.080 --> 00:00:48.782 align:start size:94% position:6%
and all of it went
over his head.

00:00:48.782 --> 00:00:52.052 align:start size:94% position:6%
But he loved it.
Which I was thrilled.

00:00:52.052 --> 00:00:55.055 align:start size:94% position:6%
In fact, we give him
an allowance and he has, like,

00:00:55.055 --> 00:00:57.290 align:start size:94% position:6%
saving, donating,
and spending,

00:00:57.290 --> 00:00:58.892 align:start size:94% position:6%
and he saved up
for the longest time

00:00:58.892 --> 00:01:01.127 align:start size:94% position:6%
and he bought
an "Austin Powers" costume.

00:01:01.127 --> 00:01:04.130 align:start size:94% position:6%
[ Laughter ]
And he does it all the time.

00:01:04.130 --> 00:01:06.499 align:start size:94% position:6%
And I was like,
"You know, is this weird?"

00:01:06.499 --> 00:01:07.801 align:start size:94% position:6%
He goes, "No, no,
I think it's great."

00:01:07.801 --> 00:01:10.804 align:start size:94% position:6%
And then, we were somewhere,
and it was raining

00:01:10.804 --> 00:01:11.871 line:92%
and we were under a blanket.

00:01:11.871 --> 00:01:14.307 align:start size:94% position:6%
And he said, "Dada,
can I tell you a secret?"

00:01:14.307 --> 00:01:15.341 line:92%
And I said, "Sure, Spike, what?"

00:01:15.341 --> 00:01:17.811
And he goes... [whispers]
"I'm your number one fan."

00:01:17.811 --> 00:01:18.778 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
[ Audience "aw"s ]

00:01:18.778 --> 00:01:22.115 align:start size:94% position:6%
And I was like, "Oh, my God."
[ Applause ]

00:01:22.115 --> 00:01:24.117 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
-Yeah.

00:01:24.117 --> 00:01:25.585 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
-Heart --

00:01:25.585 --> 00:01:27.887
Chest not big enough for heart.
-Yeah.

00:01:27.887 --> 00:01:29.889 align:start size:94% position:6%
-It's just the happiest time
of my life.

00:01:29.889 --> 00:01:31.458 align:start size:94% position:6%
These kids are fantastic,
all of them, so...

00:01:31.458 --> 00:01:33.460 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yeah, it's --
I agree with that.

00:01:33.460 --> 00:01:34.394 size:75% position:38% line:92%
I did not know this.

00:01:34.394 --> 00:01:37.130 size:75% position:38%
And I'm so now angry
that I wasn't there.

00:01:37.130 --> 00:01:40.400
One performance -- you did one
performance with Fred Armisen.

00:01:40.400 --> 00:01:41.334 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yes.
-In a band.

00:01:41.334 --> 00:01:43.269 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yeah.
-Called the Modern Weepers.

00:01:43.269 --> 00:01:44.037 size:75% position:38% line:92%
-The Modern Weepers.

00:01:44.037 --> 00:01:46.539 align:start size:94% position:6%
Yeah, we wanted to do
a mope rock band.

00:01:46.539 --> 00:01:48.508 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yeah.
-That sort of like --

00:01:48.508 --> 00:01:49.309 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
-So like, emo-y?

00:01:49.309 --> 00:01:50.910 align:start size:94% position:6%
Like, what would be
the inspirations?

00:01:50.910 --> 00:01:52.312 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Like The Cure --
-Okay.

00:01:52.312 --> 00:01:52.879 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
-Human League.

00:01:52.879 --> 00:01:54.280 size:81% position:41%
It's this sort of band
that's like, you know,

00:01:54.280 --> 00:01:55.815 align:start size:94% position:6%
[ British accent ]
"You know, we're very sad

00:01:55.815 --> 00:01:57.717 align:start size:94% position:6%
to be here tonight."
[ Laughter ]

00:01:57.717 --> 00:01:58.418 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
-There's Fred.

00:01:58.418 --> 00:01:59.786 align:start size:94% position:6%
There's Fred
and the Modern Weepers.

00:01:59.786 --> 00:02:01.955 size:81% position:41%
-You were Hugh, right?
-Yeah, that's right.

00:02:01.955 --> 00:02:03.389 align:start size:94% position:6%
-What was your name?
-Hugh.

00:02:03.389 --> 00:02:06.192 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Hugh. And what was your name?
-I can't remember.

00:02:06.192 --> 00:02:07.127 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
-What was that --

00:02:07.127 --> 00:02:08.461 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Do you remember
any of the songs you did?

00:02:08.461 --> 00:02:09.696 align:start size:94% position:6%
Like, the titles?
-Yeah, yeah.

00:02:09.696 --> 00:02:11.030 align:start size:94% position:6%
"Cry Pail."
-"Cry Pail."

00:02:11.030 --> 00:02:12.966
-[ British accent ]
♪♪ Every time I see your face ♪♪

00:02:12.966 --> 00:02:16.236 align:start size:94% position:6%
♪♪ I cry in a pail ♪♪
[ Laughter ]

00:02:16.236 --> 00:02:18.204 line:92%
♪♪ You deliciously rejected me ♪♪

00:02:18.204 --> 00:02:19.572 size:81% position:41% line:92%
♪♪ I cry and I wail ♪♪

00:02:19.572 --> 00:02:22.242
And the other one is "Don't Ask
Me Personal Questions."

00:02:22.242 --> 00:02:23.343 align:start size:94% position:6%
You remember that?
-Yeah.

00:02:23.343 --> 00:02:26.179 size:84% position:42%
-"Pasta and Red Sauce."
-"Pasta and Red Sauce"?

00:02:26.179 --> 00:02:28.548 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yes. "Pasta and Red Sauce."
-[ Laughs ]

00:02:28.548 --> 00:02:31.518 align:start size:94% position:6%
-"Embrace" --
-"The Girls of New York."

00:02:31.518 --> 00:02:33.620 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yeah.
-What's another one?

00:02:33.620 --> 00:02:35.088 align:start size:94% position:6%
I think it was
"Catalog of Misery."

00:02:35.088 --> 00:02:36.856 align:start size:94% position:6%
Something like that. It was --
-Yeah.

00:02:36.856 --> 00:02:40.226 align:start size:94% position:6%
-All sad songs.
-One night only in L.A.?

00:02:40.226 --> 00:02:41.194 align:start size:94% position:6%
-New York.
-New York.

00:02:41.194 --> 00:02:42.562 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Oh, New York.
-Mercury Lounge, yeah.

00:02:42.562 --> 00:02:43.663 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Fantastic.
And that was it.

00:02:43.663 --> 00:02:45.965 align:start size:94% position:6%
That was the end
of the Modern Weepers.

00:02:45.965 --> 00:02:47.433 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Pretty much, yeah.
-Yeah.

00:02:47.433 --> 00:02:49.936
-Well, that's the situation
where unlike George Harrison,

00:02:49.936 --> 00:02:52.238 size:78% position:39%
you might not have to
tell your son that.

00:02:52.238 --> 00:02:53.339 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
-Yes. I --

00:02:53.339 --> 00:02:54.974 line:92%
-"Dad, are you a Modern Weeper?"

00:02:54.974 --> 00:02:57.010 align:start size:94% position:6%
-"Why didn't you tell me?"
-[ Laughs ]

00:02:57.010 --> 00:02:58.745 align:start size:94% position:6%
-"Because it's kind of
a big thing."

00:02:58.745 --> 00:03:00.013 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Thanks so much
for being here, Mike.

00:03:00.013 --> 00:03:01.114 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Thank you so much
for having me.

00:03:01.114 --> 00:03:02.682 align:start size:94% position:6%
-It's always such a pleasure
to see you.

00:03:02.682 --> 00:03:04.217 size:81% position:41% line:92%
Mike Myers, everybody!

